      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Foods with a high glycemic index cause your blood sugar and insulin levels to spike rapidly, which can overwhelm insulin resistance in type 2 diabetes and lead to energy crashes. In contrast, low glycemic index foods digest slowly, providing a gradual rise in blood sugar that helps maintain stable energy and reduces the demand for insulin. Incorporating more low-GI foods, such as whole grains and non-starchy vegetables, into your diet is a key strategy for managing glucose levels alongside medication.",
