      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A stable breakfast might include Greek yogurt with berries and a slice of whole-grain toast, as the protein in the yogurt pairs well with the complex carbohydrates in the toast to slow digestion. For lunch, consider a large salad with chickpeas, quinoa, and olive oil dressing instead of relying on white bread, apples, or sugary cereals. These combinations prioritize fiber and complex carbs to avoid the sharp sugar spikes associated with high-GI items. Consistently choosing these food pairings at every meal can make managing your type 2 diabetes much easier and more sustainable.",
      "source": "target",
